    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A small Pyrenean state created in 1278 when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bishop">bishop</a> of Urgell and the count of Foix agreed to share its lordship.</li><li>For centuries a poor community of herders and smugglers, it kept its autonomy by staying neutral between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#spain">Spain</a>.</li><li>A constitution in 1993 made it a sovereign parliamentary co-principality; it joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#united-nations">United Nations</a> the same year.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Andorra is the only country where Catalan is the sole official language, and one of its two heads of state is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#bishop">bishop</a> of a Spanish diocese.</p></aside>
    </section>

